in-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "score": 0.26, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF13 (0.15)", "request matches LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean (0.15); FAM:SF13 auto_limited_by LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Within-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Offenses that shift toward the counter play types for the inferred opponent scheme gain PPP later in the game.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-003] 531 rows with inferred scheme; 249 adapted (46.9%); adapters +0.0701 (n=239) vs non-adapters +0.0121 (n=269), advantage +0.0580 PPP; DROP +0.1001, SWITCH -0.0436, HELP +0.0450.", "[APPM-013] Adapter dPPP +0.0613 vs +0.0131; advantage +0.0482 PPP, p=0.0199. SWITCH subgroup reversed (-0.0160).", "[CHT-018] First run: adapters n=229 mean dPPP +0.0613 vs non-adapters; later 586 rows, 90.6% inferable, adapters +0.0701 vs non-adapters +0.0121, lift +0.058 (n=508). T1: no-signal baseline is highest dPPP so +0.05 lift  [cut; read_family for the full text]"]}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}]}], "n_results": 4}

